    {
      "table": "6.4",
      "position": 2,
      "ids": [
        "account.signIn"
      ],
      "cells": [
        "`account.signIn({ method: \"device_code\" \\| \"browser\", open_browser?, onUserCode, onOpenUrl?, deviceName?, replace?, signal? })`. The codes go to `onUserCode` in a `code` event; the result is the `signed_in` content (api, device, replaced device, device-service outcome) or a typed refusal. `method: \"browser\"` is the callback flow of `omo login`; `open_browser: false` is `--no-browser`. While accounts are closed only `device_code` is admitted and every other combination is the refusal the CLI gives today. Two CLI projections of the one call: `omo login` renders the `code` event as its three lines; `omo account sign-in` renders each event as one JSON line",
        "`omo login [--device] [--no-browser] [--replace] [--api] [--accounts]`; `omo account sign-in [--stdin]`",
        "none",
        "partial: device code only, and it runs the CLI as a child (`S/account/sign-in-process.ts`)",
        "Tool omitted: a sign-in needs a person at a browser. The SDK stops running the CLI; the CLI calls the SDK",
        "A1b, after S0"
      ]
    },
